<title>JAPAN: Nihon Unicom to buy back 310,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Nihon Unicom to buy back 310,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nihon Unicom Corp, a specialised futures trader, said on Thursday it has decided to buy back 310,000 of its own shares to introduce a stock option scheme.</p>
<p>The amount of the share repurchase would be 500 million yen, the company said.  </p>
<p>The decision must be approved by a shareholders' meeting scheduled for June 27.</p>
<p>The stock options will be offered to 15 board directors and 32 executives. The repurchase will be carried out from July 1, 1998, to September 30, 2000, Nihon Unicom said.</p>
</text>
